        {
          "id": "bd3e343c-d528-319a-9b35-6c589269896e",
          "content": {
            "id": "bd3e343c-d528-319a-9b35-6c589269896e",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "EasyJet says summer bookings rising after\u00a0wider quarterly loss",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: British budget airline easyJet said summer bookings were building strongly, despite reporting a wider first-quarter loss on Thursday.</p><p>The company has been hit by expansion costs and soft winter pricing.</p><p>Winter is typically the weakest period for airlines.</p><p>Carriers rely on spring and summer demand to lift earnings.</p><p>The company said the busy January booking period has seen record levels in both volume and revenue ahead of summer 2026.\u00a0</p><p>But the airline reported an operating loss of around $105 million in the three months to December 31.</p><p>That's compared with around a $55 million loss a year earlier.</p><p>Despite this, the airline kept its 2026 outlook unchanged with shares rising\u00a02% in early trading.</p><p>Separately, Wizz Air reported a third-quarter operating loss in line with expectations.</p><p>Earlier this week, larger rival Ryanair raised its fare growth outlook after a strong start to 2026 bookings.</p><p>Budget carriers have sidestepped many of the challenges facing Europe's biggest airlines.</p><p>Which have been squeezed by weaker transatlantic travel linked to tariff threats from U.S. President Donald Trump.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: British budget airline easyJet said summer bookings were building strongly, despite reporting a wider first-quarter loss on Thursday.</p><p>The company has been hit by expansion costs and soft winter pricing.</p><p>Winter is typically the weakest period for airlines.</p><p>Carriers rely on spring and summer demand to lift earnings.</p><p>The company said the busy January booking period has seen record levels in both volume and revenue ahead of summer 2026.&nbsp;</p><p>But the airline reported an operating loss of around $105 million in the three months to December 31.</p><p>That's compared with around a $55 million loss a year earlier.</p><p>Despite this, the airline kept its 2026 outlook unchanged with shares rising&nbsp;2% in early trading.</p><p>Separately, Wizz Air reported a third-quarter operating loss in line with expectations.</p><p>Earlier this week, larger rival Ryanair raised its fare growth outlook after a strong start to 2026 bookings.</p><p>Budget carriers have sidestepped many of the challenges facing Europe's biggest airlines.</p><p>Which have been squeezed by weaker transatlantic travel linked to tariff threats from U.S. President Donald Trump.</p></body>",
